---
// "How this was made": fixed copy about our own process. It makes no claim about any inductee.
// Links to the public fact log exports (src/pages/data/[file].js: verified records only).
// The room credits are read from the manifests that ship (content/scans/<id>.json, the
// study-corner records), so this page cannot describe rooms the site no longer shows.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { listChapters, loadChapter, loadScan, listInductees, loadStudyCorner, usedScanIds } from '../content/load.js';
import { loadHall } from '../content/hall.js';

// Every scanned room a page shows, with where it is used (the rooms the production build ships:
// usedScanIds).
const uses = new Map(usedScanIds().map(id => [id, new Set()]));
const hall = loadHall();
if (hall && hall.scan) uses.get(hall.scan).add('the hallway');
for (const { slug, n } of listChapters()) {
  const room = loadChapter(slug, n).room;
  if (room && typeof room === 'object' && room.scan) uses.get(room.scan).add('the chapter rooms');
}
const rooms = [...uses].map(([id, where]) => ({ m: loadScan(id), where: [...where].join(' and ') }));
const masked = n => (n ? `${n} region${n === 1 ? '' : 's'} covered with a flat colour` : 'nothing covered');

// The recreated study corners: which pieces come from a model kit, which we made.
const words = k => k.replace(/-/g, ' ');
const corners = listInductees().map(loadStudyCorner).filter(Boolean).map(c => {
  const models = c.models || {};
  const included = new Set(Object.values(models).flatMap(m => m.includes || []));
  const kit = c.objects.filter(o => o.model).map(o => words(o.kind) + ((models[o.model].includes || []).length ? ` (with its ${models[o.model].includes.map(words).join(', ')})` : ''));
  const ours = c.objects.filter(o => !o.model && !included.has(o.id)).map(o => words(o.kind));
  const used = new Set(Object.values(models).map(m => m.source));
  return { label: c.label, kit, ours, sources: (c.sources || []).filter(s => used.has(s.id)) };
});
const list = xs => (xs.length < 2 ? xs.join('') : `${xs.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and ${xs[xs.length - 1]}`);
---
<Base title="How this was made" description="How the facts, scanned rooms, portraits and voices in IHH: Voices of Arrival were made and checked.">
  <article class="method">
    <h1>How this was made</h1>
    <p class="lede">Every sentence, label and caption in these rooms comes from a fact we can show you. This page explains how
      those facts were collected and checked, and what the rooms, portraits and voices are made of.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="facts">
      <h2 id="facts">Facts first</h2>
      <p>Each fact is one short claim, stored with the exact words from its source, a link to that source and a saved copy of
        the page. An AI agent searches archives, libraries, museums and government records and extracts candidate facts.</p>
      <p>A second AI model then checks every fact on its own: a different model, run in a separate session, that sees the
        claim and the evidence but never the first model's reasoning, and is told to refute the fact if it can. Automatic
        checks confirm that the quoted words really appear in the saved source and that the source is the kind it claims to be.</p>
      <p>A fact is used only when both models agree and every check passes. When they disagree, nothing is published on its
        own: the fact waits for a person to decide.</p>
      <p>Before the site is built, a final check compares every sentence with the facts it cites. A sentence that contains a
        word, date or number its facts do not contain stops the build. Quotes must match their source word for word.</p>
      <p>Next to each sentence, a <strong>Source</strong> button opens the source's title, holder, date and link.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="evidence">
      <h2 id="evidence">Evidence tiers</h2>
      <dl class="tiers">
        <dt>Verified</dt>
        <dd>Backed by the original record itself, or by two independent holders, at least one of them an archive, library,
          museum or government body. Only verified facts appear on this site.</dd>
        <dt>Single source</dt>
        <dd>Found in one source only. Not shown.</dd>
        <dt>Disputed</dt>
        <dd>Sources or checks disagree. Not shown.</dd>
        <dt>Rejected</dt>
        <dd>Failed a check. Not shown.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>Exhibits carry one of three labels: <strong>Original record</strong> (a scan of the document),
        <strong>Original photograph</strong>, or <strong>Reconstruction</strong> (made by us, always with a link to the original).</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rooms">
      <h2 id="rooms">The rooms are scans of real rooms</h2>
      <p>The rooms you walk through are 3D scans of historic rooms in Swedish museums, published by the museums themselves
        under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence (CC BY 4.0). They are not places any inductee lived or worked in,
        and the museums are not connected to the Immigrant Hall of Honor or its inductees; each room says so on its label.</p>
      <ul class="credits">
        {rooms.map(({ m, where }) => (
          <li><strong>{m.place}</strong>, used for {where}. Published by {m.publisher}:
            <a href={m.sketchfab_url}>{m.title}</a>, <a href={m.licence_url}>{m.licence}</a>; {masked((m.crops || []).length)}.
            <span class="credit-text">{m.credit}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>What we changed is listed in each credit. We stood each room upright and centred it, set its scale from a height
        we could check (a table top or a seat), simplified and recompressed the mesh for the web (more for phones), and
        resized, colour-balanced and recompressed its photographs. The room is shown as it was photographed, without our lighting: the light you see is
        the light the museum's scan recorded. A small preview loads first, then the full room for your device.</p>
      <p>Before a room was used, we listed every painting, tapestry and painted or carved piece visible in the scan and
        matched each to the museum's catalogue record. A work is shown only if its artist died more than 70 full years ago
        or, with no known artist, the catalogue dates it at least 191 years back, so no one who made it can still hold a
        copyright. Anything that does not clear, and any modern sign we could read, is covered with a flat colour in the
        files we ship. Rooms where too much could not be cleared are not used. The build refuses a room whose list has
        changed since it was reviewed, or whose files differ from the ones reviewed.</p>
      <p>Our own exhibits stand on easels and stands we model, lit to sit with the scan. Letters and documents shown in 3D
        are a sheet of paper we model, printed with the holder's scan. The original record is always one link away.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="reconstructions">
      <h2 id="reconstructions">The recreated study corner</h2>
      {corners.map(c => (
        <>
          <p>In one room, a corner is set out like a study shown in two archive photographs ({c.label.replace(/^Recreation based on photographs: /, '')}).
            It is a recreation, not the room in the photographs. We placed only the kinds of furniture the photographs show,
            at sizes and positions estimated from them. The pieces are modern stand-ins, not the original designs: the
            {' '}{list(c.kit)} come from a ready-made furniture kit, each used on its own and resized, and the {list(c.ours)} are
            simple shapes we generate. The kit's paintings, whose origin and rights are unknown, are never shipped.</p>
          <ul class="credits">
            {c.sources.map(s => (
              <li><a href={s.url}>{s.title}</a> by {s.author}, <a href={s.licence_url}>{s.licence}</a>. {s.changes}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </>
      ))}
      <p>The corner's plaque names the photographs it is based on, with their holder and date, and links to each untouched
        original ("See the original").</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="portraits">
      <h2 id="portraits">Painted portraits</h2>
      <p>Each portrait is painted by our own software filter from an archive photograph that is in the public domain or under
        an open licence. The filter repaints the photograph's own pixels; no face, expression or feature is generated.</p>
      <p>The slight movement comes from a depth estimate made by an AI model (Depth Anything V2 Small, Apache-2.0 licence),
        which shifts the painting in layers. The mouth never moves. If your device asks for reduced motion, the portrait stays
        still, and you can pause the motion at any time.</p>
      <p>The people shown did not pose for or approve these paintings. Each portrait names the holder and date of the photograph it was made from.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="voices">
      <h2 id="voices">Voices</h2>
      <p>The guide's narration and the spoken quotes use AI-generated voices from Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0 licence), generated
        in advance on our own computer, not live. They are stock voices that come with the model; none is cloned from, or made to imitate, a real
        person's recordings.</p>
      <p>A quote voice reads only a cited quote, word for word, and is labeled "AI-generated voice, not [name]'s voice", with
        the source and date of the words. Every recording has captions and a written transcript.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights">
      <h2 id="rights">Images and rights</h2>
      <p>We show an image only when its holder marks it public domain or under a CC0, CC BY or CC BY-SA licence. Credits and
        rights statements are shown in the holder's exact wording. Anything else is linked, not shown.</p>
      <p>The optional room sound is brown noise generated by our own script; no recording is used. It is off until you turn it on.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="globe">
      <h2 id="globe">Journey globe</h2>
      <p>The Earth on each journey page is NASA's Blue Marble: Next Generation (July 2004, with topography and bathymetry), from
        <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/blue-marble-next-generation/base-topography-bathymetry/">NASA Visible Earth / Blue Marble</a>.
        As a work of NASA it is in the public domain in the United States; we only resized it. NASA does not endorse this project.</p>
      <p>A stop gets a pin only when one of its cited facts names the place. The pin sits at that place's published coordinates
        (from Wikidata, linked from each stop), so its position is approximate and is not a claim about where exactly anyone stood.
        The travel lines join the pins in order along the shortest path over the globe; they show sequence, not the route taken.
        Without 3D, or if your device asks for reduced motion, the same stops appear on a flat drawn map.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="typeface">
      <h2 id="typeface">Typeface</h2>
      <p>The home page, the timelines and the site's header and footer are set in Poppins (Copyright 2020 The Poppins Project
        Authors, Indian Type Foundry), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. We serve the font files from this site, from the
        Fontsource 5.3.0 build; no font is loaded from another host. The licence text is at
        <a href="/fonts/poppins/OFL.txt">/fonts/poppins/OFL.txt</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="fact-log">
      <h2 id="fact-log">The fact log</h2>
      <p>These files list the verified facts and media used across the project, with their sources, evidence quotes and the
        results of each check. Candidates that are not verified are left out. Every fact and media row names its
        review state; only rows marked approved or edited have passed review by the Immigrant Hall of Honor team, and rows marked
        pending have not yet been reviewed.</p>
      <ul class="downloads">
        <li><a href="/data/facts.csv" download>Facts (CSV)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/data/sources.csv" download>Sources (CSV)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/data/media.csv" download>Media (CSV)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/data/provenance.jsonld" download>Provenance (JSON-LD, schema.org and PROV-O)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .method { padding: var(--space-4); max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.55; }
  .method h1, .method h2 { font-family: var(--f-serif); }
  .method h2 { margin-top: var(--space-6); scroll-margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .method .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .method .tiers dt { font-weight: bold; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .method .tiers dd { margin: var(--space-1) 0 0; }
  .method a { color: var(--c-accent); }
  .method .downloads a { display: inline-block; min-height: 24px; padding: var(--space-1) 0; }
  .method .credits li { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .method .credit-text { display: block; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--c-muted); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
